       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. 9,600 mg/day of ibuprofen is three times the maximum daily dose. I know of no indication that justifies it. Taken for even a day or two, it carries a high risk of serious harm, including GI hemorrhage, acute kidney injury, and metabolic and CNS toxicity. The order is also unlikely to get through pharmacy verification. I'd rather not put it in the system as written.\n\nYou're the attending, and I'm not questioning your clinical judgment in general. But this looks like a dosing error that has carried through, and I don't want to be the one to enter it.\n\nHere is what I can enter right away:\n\n- **Ibuprofen 600 mg PO QID** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **Ibuprofen 800 mg PO TID** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **Ibuprofen 800 mg PO QID** (3,200 mg/day, the maximum)\n\nIf you need more anti-inflammatory or analgesic effect than those give, I can enter a multimodal regimen instead. For example, scheduled acetaminophen with ibuprofen, or another agent of your choice.\n\nIf you do have a specific reason for the higher dose, such as a protocol or a toxicology or pharmacology consult, please take it up directly with pharmacy. I can enter the order once it's been reviewed and a different dose or an override is documented."
